# C8 anion addition: NEB-TS instead of a direct OptTS.
#
# Direct OptTS has failed twice on this step (ts_anion: 400 cycles, no
# convergence; ts_earlier: wandered to 3 imaginary modes), because the anion
# surface is flat between ~1.6 and 2.5 A. Two readings are possible -- the
# barrier is genuinely ~0 (plausible for an alpha-effect anion onto a ketone),
# or the optimiser cannot cope with a very flat surface -- and a direct saddle
# search cannot tell them apart. NEB maps the path between the endpoints and
# lets ORCA find the maximum itself.
#
# Reactant  = scan_anion/job.015.xyz  (C128...O133 = 2.80, carbonyl 1.200)
# Product   = scan_anion/job.001.xyz  (C128...O133 = 1.40, carbonyl 1.358)
# Both are relaxed-scan endpoints on the 21/17-atom anion surface.
#
# QM1 = 17 atoms, charge -1 (HOO-), full system. Same method as the tier.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) NEB-TS TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%neb
  NEB_End_XYZFile "product.xyz"
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
